Package: LogisNormIntegral
Title: Certified Minimax Approximation of the Logistic-Normal Integral
Version: 0.2.7
Authors@R:
    person("Ruijie", "Li", , "ruijie@leefy.net",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Evaluate the logistic-normal integral, the expectation of a
    logistic sigmoid under a Gaussian argument, via certified K-term minimax
    normal-scale mixture approximations for K = 1, ..., 11, relaxed
    Bernstein-Akhiezer certificates at K = 14 to 17, and a certified
    signed K = 22 frontier (Delta = 3.6e-15), with error guaranteed below a
    certified bound Delta_K*. The normal-scale-mixture approximation follows
    Monahan and Stefanski (1992, ISBN:9780824785871), resting on the exact
    scale-mixture representation of the logistic distribution given by Andrews
    and Mallows (1974) <doi:10.1111/j.2517-6161.1974.tb00989.x> and Stefanski
    (1991) <doi:10.1016/0167-7152(91)90181-P>. Weights and scales for
    K = 1, ..., 11 are the certified global minimax, with equioscillation and
    global uniqueness proved via varisolvency (see the package vignette).
    Also provides asymptotic series, from the duality with the Mordell
    integrals of Zwegers (2002) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.0807.4834>, for analytical
    work in small- and large-variance regimes.
